{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018669-idea-monthly-content-subscription","id":1018669,"title":"Idea: Monthly Content Subscription","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-17T20:45:53-08:00","id":1018669,"title":"Idea: Monthly Content Subscription","content":"This is me pitching ideas into the void, in the hopes of hearing some thoughts from fellow fans and maybe something out of someone official, but: what's the interest like in the idea of small batches of monthly paid content? <br /> <br /> If you look at the success of Patreons from various RPG authors and zines or Pelgrane Press' <i>Ken Writes About Stuff </i>series, there's a decent market out there for small batches of monthly paid content. I have to wonder if such a model might be something worth considering for OPP, as it solves the unceasing hunger among the fans for blog posts without demanding lots of unpaid work from various writers done in their free time and allows an easy means for stuff like 2e updates for Bloodlines/Lodges/Legacies or random batches of new mechanics, standalone antagonists, and whatever else. There's a fear of both bloated supplements and going long stretches of time without anything for a given game under the CofD umbrella, and it's one that feels brilliant to my currently sleep-deprived little brain.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on this hypothetical model?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T21:27:36-08:00","id":1018681,"title":"","content":"This is something that has popped into my head pretty much every time discussions about what to do about the financial side of the business comes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T22:10:55-08:00","id":1018690,"title":"","content":"More ways to get CofD content and more ways to support Onyx Path are both good things in my book. So yeah, I'd sub to something like this if they put it out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T00:22:38-08:00","id":1018723,"title":"","content":"I like the idea. I hear so many here clamoring for Bloodline, Legacy; Lodge etc. updates that a monthly sub kind of thing for this kind of material and more would be great to have. I see some of the Freelanacers put up their notes and home table info that giving them a little extra scratch would be a way to show our appreciation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T01:08:49-08:00","id":1018731,"title":"","content":"I wonder how a monthly cycle would fit in with WW's right of review.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T01:20:41-08:00","id":1018732,"title":"","content":"/bites tongue on business-consultancy-type commentary<br /> <br /> I would totally sign up for this if I could filter out stuff I'm not interested in. Depending on how much is what, I might even be willing to pay for stuff that I'm not interested in in order to get the stuff I am interested in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T01:31:29-08:00","id":1018734,"title":"","content":"I'd pay for it. I thinl it would be a great idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T03:41:51-08:00","id":1018759,"title":"","content":"It would be a nice way to give lines material when the next book is ages away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T03:47:54-08:00","id":1018760,"title":"","content":"The cost should be adequate to the content, though. Remember that a book costs around 15-20 dollars for 150-300 pages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T04:10:08-08:00","id":1018762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018669-idea-monthly-content-subscription?p=1018760#post1018760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The cost should be adequate to the content, though. Remember that a book costs around 15-20 dollars for 150-300 pages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it'd be should be much higher than 10 cents a page because of it coming out so regularly and it being an addition to the schedule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 12-18-2016, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T04:15:55-08:00","id":1018764,"title":"","content":"Higher? Yes. But being addition or not it shouldn't be overpiced like most of the DLC's nowadays.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T13:09:28-08:00","id":1018877,"title":"","content":"I would pay for this.<br /> I <b>want</b> to pay for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T13:37:16-08:00","id":1018885,"title":"","content":"While I like the idea, I'm not sure it'd work. One problem with a subscription model is that it basically forces the writers and developers to constantly be making new content due to a looming deadline - this can cause them to become stressed out from a) trying to make new, balanced content, and b) finding all the vague language, typos and plain errata mistakes before sending it out. Then there's also figuring out what content to split into parts so they have a backlog to submit to players to avoid problems A and B. We'd be asking the gamedevs to make stuff they'd normally have months to test and work out to less than a month to make, draft up and fine-tune.<br /> <br /> Now, if they had a <i>fiction</i> subscription, possibly one like Demon: Interface, which has new merits and powers for player characters of various splats to take, that I'd be fine with, because it'd not just offer up new content in a decent feed, it'd also provide a narrative that would give context for how that power/item works in-universe. Of course, the problem with that is getting an appropriate number of authors to regularly churn out content, and making the content the story shows off, which still runs into problems A and B.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T14:11:54-08:00","id":1018896,"title":"","content":"I like the idea, but then I remember that Onyx Path is mostly made up from Freelancers that do this as a side job, and even Wizards of the Coast has problems keeping up with monthly content for their DND 5e. It sounds easy, but is actually hard to do unless you can dedicate a whole team to do this as their fulltime job.<br /> That, or you will end up with a medicore material. Probably easiest thing to produce would be short adventures, and they have obvious problems of Chronicles being modular and hard to pinpoint the &quot;unified universal experience&quot; you would have to write for. Fictions is another good bet...but that's dangerously close to dreaded metaplot.<br /> <br /> And remember, CofD is multiple lines published at once. You would have to either do something universal each month, do a content for EACH GAMELINE each month (imagine how many teams it would require), or make people like me not subscribe because I don't care about non-Mage stuff and I would not subscribe for Promethean or Werewolf materials.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> And as open dev showed many times, writing up inspired and balanced mechanics for CofD can be *hard*. Imagine forcing a group of people to spawn these once per month with minimal time to playtest these things. It would be...very...potentially...you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 12-18-2016, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T14:26:01-08:00","id":1018900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018669-idea-monthly-content-subscription?p=1018896#post1018896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea, but then I remember that Onyx Path is mostly made up from Freelancers that do this as a side job, and even Wizards of the Coast has problems keeping up with monthly content for their DND 5e. It sounds easy, but is actually hard to do unless you can dedicate a whole team to do this as their fulltime job.<br /> That, or you will end up with a medicore material. Probably easiest thing to produce would be short adventures, and they have obvious problems of Chronicles being modular and hard to pinpoint the &quot;unified universal experience&quot; you would have to write for. Fictions is another good bet...but that's dangerously close to dreaded metaplot.<br /> <br /> And remember, CofD is multiple lines published at once. You would have to either do something universal each month, do a content for EACH GAMELINE each month (imagine how many teams it would require), or make people like me not subscribe because I don't care about non-Mage stuff and I would not subscribe for Promethean or Werewolf materials.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> And as open dev showed many times, writing up inspired and balanced mechanics for CofD can be *hard*. Imagine forcing a group of people to spawn these once per month with minimal time to playtest these things. It would be...very...potentially...you know.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) All of this true.<br /> <br /> 2) On the other hand, there's a fair number of writers that do have material that they'd love to get out there but don't neccesarily have a place to. Often times, it becomes a question of &quot;hold onto this for a prospective book that may never come&quot; or &quot;release it as blog/forum material and never get paid for it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of these two, point 1 wins out. 2 just has to at least be pointed at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T14:34:36-08:00","id":1018906,"title":"","content":"There's also the thought that you could just buy individual releases later on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T14:51:36-08:00","id":1018919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018669-idea-monthly-content-subscription?p=1018900#post1018900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) All of this true.<br /> <br /> 2) On the other hand, there's a fair number of writers that do have material that they'd love to get out there but don't neccesarily have a place to. Often times, it becomes a question of &quot;hold onto this for a prospective book that may never come&quot; or &quot;release it as blog/forum material and never get paid for it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of these two, point 1 wins out. 2 just has to at least be pointed at.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Best shot at this would be draft up something like a plan for 12 months of releases, assign goals and do some general planning, and then start with a emergency backlog of 1-2 releases in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T14:59:10-08:00","id":1018926,"title":"","content":"It could be less frequently than monthly. A quarterly, or even yearly release would still be something, and would leave more time to develop the content.<br /> <br /> Alternatively (or perhaps additionally), it could come with a big honking &quot;this has not been through playtesting and development&quot; disclaimer. That's how WotC has been doing their Unearthed Arcana blog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-18-2016, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T15:01:21-08:00","id":1018927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018669-idea-monthly-content-subscription?p=1018926#post1018926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be less frequently than monthly. A quarterly, or even yearly release would still be something, and would leave more time to develop the content.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd pay for a quarterly thing. A good balance between frequency and lead time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T16:10:04-08:00","id":1018949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018669-idea-monthly-content-subscription?p=1018896#post1018896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea, but then I remember that Onyx Path is mostly made up from Freelancers that do this as a side job, and even Wizards of the Coast has problems keeping up with monthly content for their DND 5e. It sounds easy, but is actually hard to do unless you can dedicate a whole team to do this as their fulltime job.<br /> That, or you will end up with a medicore material. Probably easiest thing to produce would be short adventures, and they have obvious problems of Chronicles being modular and hard to pinpoint the &amp;quot;unified universal experience&amp;quot; you would have to write for. Fictions is another good bet...but that's dangerously close to dreaded metaplot.<br /> <br /> And remember, CofD is multiple lines published at once. You would have to either do something universal each month, do a content for EACH GAMELINE each month (imagine how many teams it would require), or make people like me not subscribe because I don't care about non-Mage stuff and I would not subscribe for Promethean or Werewolf materials.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> And as open dev showed many times, writing up inspired and balanced mechanics for CofD can be *hard*. Imagine forcing a group of people to spawn these once per month with minimal time to playtest these things. It would be...very...potentially...you know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note: All hypothetical here.<br /> <br /> So long as the expectation wasn't massive, I don't think this is as concerning as you might think. When I'm writing full-time effectively, I crank out between 50-80,000 words a month. I could easily do 5,000-10,000 on a regular basis if I knew it was lined up in advance, partly because it'd be easy to backlog a little bit, and because I could just do it between other work as an exercise. For example, when I do bloodlines for the blog, those end up being about 1,000-2,000 words. If I were doing bloodlines, for example, I could easily do 2-3 of that caliber a month without much concern. <br /> <br /> And if I were doing that with the expectation of, say, collecting and printing the lot of them after a year, I would use the opportunity to Open Dev and revise them with time. <br /> <br /> I already release a bit here and there for the hell of it. If I had pay incentive, I'd have absolutely no trouble revising that content, and giving it a second pass to make it more workable. <br /> <br /> So I don't think it's really as unrealistic as it sounds. I'm only one writer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T16:19:04-08:00","id":1018952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018669-idea-monthly-content-subscription?p=1018949#post1018949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note: All hypothetical here.<br /> <br /> So long as the expectation wasn't massive, I don't think this is as concerning as you might think. When I'm writing full-time effectively, I crank out between 50-80,000 words a month. I could easily do 5,000-10,000 on a regular basis if I knew it was lined up in advance, partly because it'd be easy to backlog a little bit, and because I could just do it between other work as an exercise. For example, when I do bloodlines for the blog, those end up being about 1,000-2,000 words. If I were doing bloodlines, for example, I could easily do 2-3 of that caliber a month without much concern.<br /> <br /> And if I were doing that with the expectation of, say, collecting and printing the lot of them after a year, I would use the opportunity to Open Dev and revise them with time.<br /> <br /> I already release a bit here and there for the hell of it. If I had pay incentive, I'd have absolutely no trouble revising that content, and giving it a second pass to make it more workable.<br /> <br /> So I don't think it's really as unrealistic as it sounds. I'm only one writer.</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest problem is just how it would have to be set up in relation to Onyx Path and White Wolf, just the general structure of the thing. And that could always be finagled out.<br /> <br /> It could be cool, giving some more financial support and regular work, creating a space where the material could get pulpier, more of a trial space, like you got in the old White Wolf Magazines whenever it did new content.<br /> <br /> Still, even if it is smaller, I am reminded of the monthly treadmill approach and the problems there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T17:06:58-08:00","id":1018967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018669-idea-monthly-content-subscription?p=1018949#post1018949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note: All hypothetical here.<br /> <br /> So long as the expectation wasn't massive, I don't think this is as concerning as you might think. When I'm writing full-time effectively, I crank out between 50-80,000 words a month. I could easily do 5,000-10,000 on a regular basis if I knew it was lined up in advance, partly because it'd be easy to backlog a little bit, and because I could just do it between other work as an exercise. For example, when I do bloodlines for the blog, those end up being about 1,000-2,000 words. If I were doing bloodlines, for example, I could easily do 2-3 of that caliber a month without much concern.<br /> <br /> And if I were doing that with the expectation of, say, collecting and printing the lot of them after a year, I would use the opportunity to Open Dev and revise them with time.<br /> <br /> I already release a bit here and there for the hell of it. If I had pay incentive, I'd have absolutely no trouble revising that content, and giving it a second pass to make it more workable.<br /> <br /> So I don't think it's really as unrealistic as it sounds. I'm only one writer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, I feel that there is a big opportunity for RPG games in the subscription based business plan. One of things that can keep RPG franchise alive is constant supply of new material; and CofD avoided a pitfall of &quot;too much bloat will make people unwilling to start exploring the CofD, as TOO MANY BOOKS are unappealing&quot; by making sure that each publication is relatively stand-alone and finished product that doesn't require completing your library with all the, say, &quot;Complete XYZ&quot; books. Open devs also showed that people are interested in periodic publications. <br /> <br /> Tricky part is balancing it, writing it in a good quality, adapting to new/different pace and method of work, and somehow convincing your market that it's worth to keep paying the subscription fee; because if you lose their trust once, it's really hard to reclaim it, even if your material is superb. <br /> <br /> I also feel that a lot of people think that writing periodic releases like this boils down basically to writing a forum homebrew once per month, and if they can do it in 30 mintues, then why writers shouldn't; it's not that easy. It takes logistic, backup plans, general direction and would probably need at least 2-3 months of prepwork to launch if you want to make sure the quality is top notch...and it's still a big risk. Maybe it should be a Kickstarter Project :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T17:09:45-08:00","id":1018968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018669-idea-monthly-content-subscription?p=1018967#post1018967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I feel that there is a big opportunity for RPG games in the subscription based business plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it really helped Paizo's Pathfinder get off the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T17:54:05-08:00","id":1018982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018669-idea-monthly-content-subscription?p=1018968#post1018968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it really helped Paizo's Pathfinder get off the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the major income draw for Paizo is their Adventure Path subscription, that is absolutely true then and now. <br /> <br /> And I would be totally happy to see Chronicles get subscription content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T18:19:19-08:00","id":1018984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018669-idea-monthly-content-subscription?p=1018952#post1018952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest problem is just how it would have to be set up in relation to Onyx Path and White Wolf, just the general structure of the thing. And that could always be finagled out.<br /> <br /> It could be cool, giving some more financial support and regular work, creating a space where the material could get pulpier, more of a trial space, like you got in the old White Wolf Magazines whenever it did new content.<br /> <br /> Still, even if it is smaller, I am reminded of the monthly treadmill approach and the problems there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it'd avoid most of the treadmill issues, because there just wouldn't be the same raw output. That period meant multiple books' worth of content a month, on immensely tight deadlines. This would alleviate almost all those concerns, while still bringing in additional content for those so inclined. <br /> <br /> But yeah, approvals might be complicated. Then again, I think that'd be something to discuss and negotiate up front, with an eye toward the implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T11:13:34-08:00","id":1019864,"title":"","content":"I like this idea a lot. However it is implemented I would Sub in a heartbeat.<br /> <br /> The complications and potential problems makes sense between how to finagle it between WW and OP and preventing the pretty terrible structure that content in a small time frame (aka the manga release structure which, I've heard, hurts WAY more than it helps for both the writers and the readers). <br /> <br /> So Idk, whether it's quarterly or what I'd sub.<br /> I guess bottom line is I love the CofD and OP and I would support them in whatever way I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T14:12:27-08:00","id":1025563,"title":"","content":"Giving this thread a minor bump in the hopes of generating some more discussion. <br /> <br /> I suppose I'm a slight rarity in that I'd appreciate content for every single gameline, whereas some folks only stick to their favorites; I'd get just as much out of a new Changeling Entitlement as I would some sample Mummy cults, but neither of those do much for the Werewolf and Werewolf only crowd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}